(apply:) started.\n25|􀟈  Test case passing 1 argument apply → true to reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:) started.\n26|􀢄  Test reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:) recorded an issue with 1 argument apply → false at RunnerCatalogLifecycleTests.swift:2032:5: Expectation failed: (state.groupAccess[label]?.loading → true) != true\n27|􀢄  Test reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:) recorded an issue with 1 argument apply → true at RunnerCatalogLifecycleTests.swift:2032:5: Expectation failed: (state.groupAccess[label]?.loading → true) != true\n28|􀢄  Test reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:) with 2 test cases failed after 0.092 seconds with 2 issues.\n29|􀢄  Test reviewR4LogoutDuringFinalStoppedInspectionMustRefuseRemoval() recorded an issue at RunnerCatalogLifecycleTests.swift:2009:5: Expectation failed: await h.installerExecutor.calls.isEmpty\n30|􀢄  Test reviewR4LogoutDuringFinalStoppedInspectionMustRefuseRemoval() recorded an issue at RunnerCatalogLifecycleTests.swift:2010:5: Expectation failed: await h.catalog.load().first?.remoteAgentID == 42\n31|􀢄  Test reviewR4LogoutDuringFinalStoppedInspectionMustRefuseRemoval() failed after 0.104 seconds with 2 issues.\n32|􀢄  Test run with 2 tests in 0 suites failed after 0.104 seconds with 4 issues.\n33|\n34|[exit 1]","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c571","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9e5-dacc-74b3-81e5-780baad0bee6"},"sequence":275,"recorded_at":1780531400000545,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d57b5cc1-8b32-4b5c-b165-7938b80d84cd","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d57b5cc1-8b32-4b5c-b165-7938b80d84cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d57b5cc1-8b32-4b5c-b165-7938b80d84cd"},"call_id":"call_01a0a9e6946274a9b2059ae5cdd431e6","text":"Read text file `/tmp/r5/logbook-rev4.md`.\n1|# Reviewer logbook — revision 4\n2|\n3|Exact candidate f2df463be1443005d9d12bbfa7b27faae64bb5a2.\n4|Eight maintained controls pass; new production-entry attacks reproduce two remaining ownership defects: logout during final launchctl inspection still starts config.sh remove, and invalidated Load/Apply leave UI loading indefinitely. Four failed assertions across three scenarios. Repeat classes R3-F3 and R3-F2; verdict changes_requested, ordinary focused rework. No code or production service changes. See task-scoped verdict, probes and logs.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c573","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9e5-dacc-74b3-81e5-780baad0bee6"},"sequence":276,"recorded_at":1780531400000547,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d57b5cc1-8b32-4b5c-b165-7938b80d84cd","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"d57b5cc1-8b32-4b5c-b165-7938b80d84cd","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d57b5cc1-8b32-4b5c-b165-7938b80d84cd"},"call_id":"call_01a0a9e695b574a3bd3e8ff0dea6fcb6","text":"Read text file `/tmp/r5/r4-outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-304bw2 — R4 immutable authority rework (developer outcome)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Revision 4 adopts the three exact rev3 reviewer probes as maintained\n6|production-entry regressions and fixes R3-F1–F3 at the root cause with two\n7|coherent immutable boundaries: a unique login incarnation shared through\n8|production auth/session composition, and an immutable Load-time editor\n9|authority consumed by Apply. Prior mutable account/catalog comparisons are\n10|replaced, not patched. Accepted registration/global installer lease,\n11|stopped-only unregister, distinct service identities, fail-closed\n12|persistence, corrected real login policy, and the existing repository\n13|editor are preserved. No production runner was stopped, re-registered, or\n14|interrupted; the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n15|\n16|## Fixes by finding\n17|\n18|### R3-F1 — immutable editor authority, relink bound to full identity\n19|- `Runners.EditorAuthority` (new): immutable server/scope/agentID/agentName/\n20|  canonical/localID tuple captured at Load, carried in `GroupAccess`.\n21|- `Runners.Flow.loadGroupAccess`: stores the authority on success, clears\n22|  the invalidated flag, publishes access with authority.\n23|- `Runners.Flow.applyGroupAccess`: when a Load established an editor, consumes\n24|  that tuple via `consumeStoredEditorAuthority` and refuses on any mismatch\n25|  (server, scope, agent, name, canonical, localID) with an explicit\n26|  invalidation requiring a new Load — never reconstructs authority from the\n27|  mutable current catalog. A direct Apply without a prior Load establishes\n28|  its own single-write start authority (session probes stay non-vacuous).\n29|- `Runners.Flow.relink`: now requires the full original server/scope/agent\n30|  identity (same-ID different-scope/host refuses with drift naming); any\n31|  successful move changes canonical and invalidates the editor; any\n32|  mismatch refusal also invalidates, so a later Apply without a fresh Load\n33|  refuses instead of falling back to current values (`editorInvalidated`).\n34|- `Runners.Action.groupAccessInvalidated` + reducer: clears the stale group\n35|  so the UI returns to an explicit Load instead of submitting a retained ID.\n36|- `removeFromApp` clears both stored authority and the invalidated flag.\n37|\n38|### R3-F2/R3-F3 — login incarnation across Load/Apply/unregister\n39|- `GitHubSessionIdentity.sessionIncarnation` (new, optional, Codable-\n40|  compatible): fresh UUID on every successful Device Flow login, preserved\n41|  on restore when the user is unchanged (legacy nil stays nil), deleted on\n42|  logout, never touched by token refresh.\n43|- `RunnerRuntime.make`: passes the same identities store instance to\n44|  `GitHubAuth.Flow`, so the incarnation is shared through production\n45|  composition, not just the UserDefaults key.\n46|- `Runners.Flow.sessionStill`: now requires userID + normalized serverHost\n47|  + incarnation equality. Logout, account/server switch, and logout +\n48|  same-account re-login all invalidate; ordinary refresh stays valid.\n49|- Applied at every async boundary: Apply pre-PUT/PUT-boundary/post-PUT/\n50|  pre-publish/error, Load pre-fetch/repos-fetch/pre-publish/error,\n51|  unregister post-token/boundary/error, and `refreshRemote` per-scope\n52|  (now via `sessionStill`, replacing manual userID/server checks).\n53|- Invalidated attempts stop silently (no writes into the new incarnation);\n54|  unregister still guarantees its epilogue so retry proceeds.\n55|\n56|## Production call sites\n57|\n58|| Fix | Call site |\n59||---|---|\n60|| R3-F1 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.loadGroupAccess)` → store `EditorAuthority` → `Runners.Flow.apply(.applyGroupAccess)` → `editorRequiresReload`/`consumeStoredEditorAuthority` → `GitHubRunnerAPIClient.setGroupRepositories`; `Runners.Flow.apply(.relinkDirectory)` → full-identity gate → `invalidateEditor` |\n61|| R3-F2 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.applyGroupAccess/.loadGroupAccess)` → `sessionStill` (incarnation) at fetch/PUT/confirm/publish/error → `fetchGroupRepositories`/`groupAccessLoaded` |\n62|| R3-F3 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.unregister)` → `runUnregister` post-token + boundary `sessionStill` (incarnation) → `RunnerInstallerService.unregister` |\n63|\n64|## Tests: 8 new, 224 total green\n65|\n66|Adopted probes (failed exit 1 with 5 assertion failures on rev3, pass now):\n67|`reviewR3SameAccountReloginDuringPutMustNotPublishAccess`,\n68|`reviewR3SameAccountReloginDuringRemoveTokenMustRefuseSideEffect`,\n69|`reviewR3RelinkMustNotRebindLoadedEditorToOtherOrg`.\n70|\n71|New bounds: `reviewR3SiblingLoadDuringReloginMustNotPublishAccess` (sibling\n72|Load with real relogin), `applySucceedsAfterTokenRefreshWithinSameLogin`\n73|(positive refresh control), `unregisterRetryInNewIncarnationSucceeds`\n74|(retry in new session), `relinkRefusesChangedScopeAndRequiresReload`\n75|(refusal + invalidated + Load recovery to original),\n76|`relinkSameIdentityMoveRequiresReload` (move invalidates + recovery).\n77|\n78|AC coverage: 18 of 19 named rows driven through production entry points\n79|(row 18, full UI paths, remains the stated manual-UI bound; no UI tests\n80|per task). Findings touched rows 11/16 and the async/session contract.\n81|\n82|## Mutant evidence: 4 narrowing, 0 survivors\n83|\n84|Tree reverted after each run (grep-verified clean, backup diff identical);\n85|focused suite re-run green afterwards. Each mutant keeps the gate present\n86|and weakens it to admit exactly one rejected subclass; a retained-gate\n87|control still passes.\n88|\n89|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named failing test | Exit |\n90||---|---|---|---|\n91|| `relink-admits-scope-drift` | Relink keeps host + agent checks, drops scope-vs-original | `relinkRefusesChangedScopeAndRequiresReload` (4 issues: catalog rewritten, PUT to other-org); `relinkRequiresSameAgent` still passes | 1 |\n92|| `apply-completion-admits-relogin` | Apply keeps pre-PUT incarnation checks, admits renewed same-account session at post-PUT + pre-publish | `reviewR3SameAccountReloginDuringPutMustNotPublishAccess` (2 issues: published + 4th request); `applyGroupAccessStopsWhenSessionChangesMidApply` still passes | 1 |\n93|| `unregister-admits-relogin` | Unregister keeps stopped + local-identity gates, admits renewed same-account session at post-token + boundary | `reviewR3SameAccountReloginDuringRemoveTokenMustRefuseSideEffect` (2 issues: installer ran + ID cleared); `unregisterRefusesRunningService` + `unregisterRevalidatesStoppedAtSideEffectBoundary` still pass | 1 |\n94|| `load-completion-admits-relogin` | Load keeps membership verification, admits renewed same-account session at repos fetch + publication | `reviewR3SiblingLoadDuringReloginMustNotPublishAccess` (2 issues: published + 3rd request); `loadGroupAccessStopsPublishingAfterMidLoadLogout` still passes | 1 |\n95|\n96|No survivors. No delete-only rows claimed as narrowing.\n97|\n98|## Validation (real exit codes)\n99|\n100|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 224\n101|  tests passed (216 R3 + 8 R4), re-run green after mutant reverts.\n102|- `python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests` → exit 0, 62 tests OK\n103|  (release machinery untouched).\n104|- `./Scripts/build.sh` → exit 0, `BUILD SUCCEEDED`;\n105|  `codesign --verify --deep --strict` → exit 0;\n106|  `1.2.0`, `works.relux.runnercontrol`, team `262RZ595FP`, fresh\n107|  candidate in `.temp/products/`.\n108|- No configured linter (no SwiftLint config); build shows only the\n109|  pre-existing pattern, none in changed files.\n110|- Production (read-only): `macbook-iv` service `state = running`,\n111|  exactly one `runsvc.sh` + one `Runner.Listener` per runner\n112|  (macbook-iv, cocoaskills); no `actions.runner.*` in\n113|  `~/Library/LaunchAgents` (manual external login OFF preserved).\n114|\n115|## Stated bounds\n116|\n117|- UI confirmation paths are manual (root CUA on the fresh candidate; no\n118|  UI tests per task). The production Flow gates behind them are covered.\n119|- An in-flight membership page loop may finish its current read after a\n120|  mid-loop login replacement; no write, confirmation read, or publication\n121|  follows (next read uses the old token against fake HTTP in tests, 401s\n122|  in production, and the error completion is suppressed by incarnation).\n123|- Catalog entries without a recorded server/scope predate the original\n124|  binding and rely on disk-vs-session checks for relink; the immutable\n125|  editor still binds canonical/localID/agent on every Load/Apply.\n126|- Concurrent wizard + catalog edits to the same group remain\n127|  last-write-wins (rev1 bound, unchanged).\n128|- A remove token minted just before a session invalidation expires\n129|  unused; the refused side effect is `config.sh remove` (proven\n130|  installer-idle).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
